# DTF tier manifest: virtual-usage  (issue #2785)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single (walking-skeleton topology; the aggregation
# guarantee this tier gates is storage-independent).
#
# Feature (#2785): a virtual repository's aggregated view over its member leaves
# is the DEDUPLICATED union of those leaves — content shared by two members is
# counted ONCE, not double-counted as sum(member_a)+sum(member_b) — AND a virtual
# repository is EDITABLE after creation: its member set can be changed (add /
# remove a member), gated by `repository:admin` on the virtual parent.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (A) DEDUP UNION — two local repos A,B each hold the SAME shared artifact bytes
#       plus a unique artifact. A virtual V over {A,B} reports the shared
#       coordinate EXACTLY ONCE and its aggregated size == the deduplicated union
#       (shared counted once), strictly LESS than the naive per-repo sum. Proven
#       against the aggregated content API and cross-checked against the DB
#       (distinct-checksum union vs raw sum) and the per-repo usage API.
#       Pre-#2785 the aggregate double-counts (== raw sum) or the listing errors.
#   (B) EDITABLE — as a repo-admin, POST a new member and DELETE it back: both
#       2xx and the change PERSISTS (DB + members API). As a member-repo writer
#       who is NOT repo-admin, the same mutations are refused 403 (the admin
#       gate, not mere access). Pre-#2785 the edit 404s/500s.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives an admin login + a non-admin user
# create/login + several maven PUTs + repeated repository/member API calls back
# to back through one admin; the base default (ON) would throttle them. A tier
# that must disable a shipped control does so explicitly (design 2.2).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
